SUMMARY:[Shorenstein Asia-Pacific Research Center (APARC)] Directional AI 
 Advice: Experimental Evidence from Healthcare
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T193000
DTSTAMP:20261021T175617Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53615287723230-53615287724255@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Generative AI is fast becoming the first-place people turn for
  expert advice. The advice it provides can be directional rather than neut
 ral\, shaped in part by the choices of its designers and regulators. When 
 clients consult AI before meeting an expert\, they carry this directional 
 advice into a relationship that once rested on the expert’s judgment alo
 ne. We study its consequences in healthcare through a large-scale preregis
 tered field experiment at a Chinese hospital\, where we randomize patient
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://aparc.fsi.stanford.edu/events/directio
 nal-ai-advice-experimental-evidence-healthcare\nLast synced: 2026-10-21 10
 :56 PDT
URL:https://aparc.fsi.stanford.edu/events/directional-ai-advice-experiment
 al-evidence-healthcare
END:VEVENT
