 est strain\;\nif others’ woe leaves you unmoved\,\nyour humanity remains
  unproved.” \n(Translation Fathali Moghaddam/Duncan Wu)\n\nThe above Far
 si poem was written by the great Persian poet Saadi Shirazi (1210-1291). B
 ani Adam literally means the children of Adam. The poem describes the inte
 rconnected nature of humankind\; we are all parts of the same whole\, limb
